  "draft_response": "Thanks for reporting this—I'm sorry for the impact on your team’s daily planning. Based on your note, the analytics dashboard regressed after the last release from under 5 seconds to ~30–45 seconds (and it eventually loads).\n\nWe’ve escalated this to our engineering team for investigation as a potential post-release performance regression. To help us pinpoint what changed and compare behavior, could you share the following?\n1) The release identifier: version number and (if possible) the release date/time when you first noticed the slowdown, plus rollout scope (all users vs specific environment).\n2) Scope of impact: does it affect all users, or only particular users/locations (e.g., office vs VPN)?\n3) Consistency: is the 30–45 seconds typical every time, or does it vary by time of day?\n4) Any observable errors/warnings during the slow load (copy/paste from the browser console or any on-screen messages).\n5) Approximate time-to-first-content/load measurement method: are you timing in the browser, or using server logs/analytics?\n\nOnce we have the above, we’ll align on the affected environment(s) and start correlating the slowdown with the release changes and recent telemetry.",
